{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792524119,"nonce":"5OvBJ9LfMfG3ia223gNJD5he/GY=","message":"Audited the existing formats and persistence paths before proceeding. Zyntax already serializes HIR through compiler::bytecode (.zbc), and embed::Snapshot packages checker state/typed AST plus optional split HIR (.zsnap). The import chain also has an in-process parsed-source cache. ZynML's benchmark runner implements a private .zbc disk-cache policy; CompiledModuleCache in typed_ast is descriptive metadata, not an active reusable persistence backend.\n\nExisting blockers remain 5e24efcb4fb48c15ac0ad0a57dee42ab4308d831fc0a4e8ea988709a4e5bf18f (incompatible HIR silently degrades to stripped AST), 8a8045f62a8012fe9976b7356ed1c01eb786fa45782c60d7987200f81cbbc708 (schema/build fingerprint coverage), and 33d51f398b3b4123f58ef51fc2d9603762339b728dd5ef7d62f219f03234a0c1 (Python build-time snapshot invalidation). This source-project stage stores complete typed bodies and does not depend on the unsafe HIR fallback.\n\nReviewed sibling Rayzor's compiler/src/compilation/artifact_cache.rs, compiler/src/ir/blade.rs and compiler/build.rs. BLADE restores MIR together with checker/cross-reference state and validates source, program/transitive dependencies, compile options and a content-derived compiler ABI. Carrying only function bodies is insufficient; source mtimes alone are insufficient; program-specific IDs/layouts must not be shared across unrelated graphs.\n\nThe uncommitted TS-specific envelope was removed. The implementation now extends the existing snapshot directory with optional shared input-validation metadata; persistence writes ordinary .zsnap files using SnapshotBuilder, and frontend integration supplies source records, a resolver callback and option/build identities. No separate TS magic/version or module payload format. Shared artifact encoding borrows declarations, and consuming snapshots moves decoded bodies. Prelowered optimized-project reuse remains separate pending the existing compatibility fixes.","files":null}]}